-- title:
--   Divisor of Ogg's modular unit at prime level
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime number, and suppose the Laurent series $u_\ell =$ `modularUnitSeries ℓ` $= \Delta \cdot \Delta_\ell^{-1}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, where $\Delta$ is the $q$-series $q\prod(1-q^n)^{24}$ and $\Delta_\ell$ is its substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$, lies in `modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $j(q^d)$ for the divisors $d$ of $\ell$. Let $v$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldBar ℓ` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, a proper valuation subring of the field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-generated inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ`, containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a principal ideal ring. Then the value at $v$ of the divisor $(\ell - 1)\bigl((\bar 0) - (\bar\infty)\bigr)$, where $(\bar\infty)$ is the place `cuspInftyBar ℓ` and $(\bar 0)$ its image `cuspZeroBar ℓ` under the Fricke involution, equals $\mathrm{ord}_v$ of the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar ℓ` obtained from $u_\ell$ by applying $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficient extension, $\mathrm{ord}_v$ being minus the logarithm of the normalised adic valuation attached to $v$. Equivalently: $\mathrm{ord}_v(u_\ell)$ is $\ell - 1$ at $\bar 0$, $1 - \ell$ at $\bar\infty$, and $0$ at every other place.
--
--   This is Ogg's computation of the divisor of the modular unit $\Delta(z)/\Delta(\ell z)$ on $X_0(\ell)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, in the pointwise form asserting the equality of two divisors place by place. It underlies the statements about the order of the cuspidal divisor class at prime level, in particular the principality results for multiples of $(\bar 0) - (\bar\infty)$ and the degree computation for the field generated by the inverse unit.
